{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Merged as 4aeb9c0fe23 (Gerrit 3436). First Windows sweep with it, run 44456347985 (job 135332660982, main at ab323f7df0c): every removed posix-api line passed or skipped except 3. (1, 2) The 2 new `test_a_crash_exit_is_described_on_both_platforms[-9-*]` cases expected \"SIGKILL\", but `signal.Signals` has no SIGKILL member on Windows, so the name is \"signal 9\"; test expectation fixed. (3) `test_opcert_producer_seam_8d8e.py::test_orchestrator_degrade_key_unregenerable_records_unsigned` no longer fails on `os.geteuid`; it now reaches a gate-snapshot path longer than MAX_PATH (\"Filename too long\"), so its line moves to `max-path.args` (halfcrazed-rubbly-whimbrel's class). Follow-up Gerrit 3443 (c3f9c1d1621); make verify passed in full, integration tier 226 passed."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1795072409090761997,"uuid":"013cd5e1-19b1-48c5-95a1-b7e6bf94301e"}